    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d465">

                <pb facs="0637" n="545" xml:id="pg545"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 103.97/127</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Food Administration Representative at London</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Sheldon</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Food
                        Administrator</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hoover</hi>)<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d465-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-03-30">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 30, 1918</hi></date>. <lb/> [<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Received 11.41 a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>139. Rhondda communicates following for you:</p>
                <p>The willingness of the American people voluntarily to reduce their consumption of
                    wheat products and the new measures you are taking to meet the emergency and
                    provide the Allies with bread are deeply appreciated. Such self-sacrifice and
                    whole-hearted effort inspire us with renewed determination.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>[<hi rendition="#small-caps">Sheldon</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d465-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d465-f1-content">
                <p>Transmitted by the Ambassador in Great Britain to the Secretary of State (No.
                    9290) for Hoover.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
